#: src/introduction.md:3
msgid ""
"Wisecrow is an intensive language-cramming toolkit built around the idea "
"that _frequency drives fluency_. It mines large multilingual subtitle and "
"translation corpora from [OPUS](https://opus.nlpl.eu) — OpenSubtitles, "
"CCAligned, CCMatrix, ParaCrawl and NLLB — and turns them into a "
"frequency-ordered flashcard deck backed by an "
"[FSRS](https://github.com/open-spaced-repetition/rs-fsrs) spaced-repetition "
"scheduler."
msgstr ""

#: src/introduction.md:11
msgid ""
"It is designed for learners who want to **front-load high-frequency "
"vocabulary** in a target language, see it in subtitle context, and review it "
"in a focused loop without leaving the terminal."
msgstr ""

#: src/introduction.md:15
msgid "What Wisecrow does"
msgstr ""

#: src/introduction.md:17
msgid ""
"**Ingests** TMX and OPUS XML alignment archives directly from OPUS, with "
"retry, decompression, and size limits."
msgstr ""

#: src/introduction.md:19
msgid ""
"**Persists** translation pairs into PostgreSQL with frequency counts and a "
"unique `(from_phrase, to_phrase)` constraint that makes re-ingestion safe."
msgstr ""

#: src/introduction.md:21
msgid ""
"**Schedules** review using FSRS, with sessions that can be paused and "
"resumed."
msgstr ""

#: src/introduction.md:22
msgid ""
"**Drills** with two TUI modes: a Leitner-style flashcard runner, and a "
"research-grade dual n-back that uses your own vocabulary as stimuli."
msgstr ""

#: src/introduction.md:24
msgid ""
"**Generates** CEFR-graded grammar rules and quizzes via Anthropic or OpenAI "
"LLM providers."
msgstr ""

#: src/introduction.md:26
msgid ""
"**Syncs** translations and grammar rules between Wisecrow instances over "
"HTTP."
msgstr ""

#: src/introduction.md:28
msgid ""
"**Augments** cards with on-demand audio (Microsoft Edge TTS) and imagery "
"(Unsplash) — both feature-gated and optional."
msgstr ""

#: src/introduction.md:31
msgid "What it is not"
msgstr ""

#: src/introduction.md:33
msgid ""
"Wisecrow is **not a translator**. It assumes the target corpora already "
"contain translations."
msgstr ""

#: src/introduction.md:35
msgid ""
"It is **not a course**. It will not teach you grammar progressively; it "
"ranks by frequency and lets you grind."
msgstr ""

#: src/introduction.md:37
msgid ""
"The web and mobile front-ends in this workspace are **early-stage**. The TUI "
"is the production interface today."
msgstr ""

