#: src/getting-started/first-ingest.md:17
msgid "2. Pull a small corpus"
msgstr ""

#: src/getting-started/first-ingest.md:19
msgid ""
"OpenSubtitles is the smallest of the three corpora and the fastest to test. "
"The `ingest` command downloads, parses, and persists in one pass."
msgstr ""

#: src/getting-started/first-ingest.md:26
msgid "What happens, in order:"
msgstr ""

#: src/getting-started/first-ingest.md:28
msgid "The CLI validates language codes and constructs OPUS URLs."
msgstr ""

#: src/getting-started/first-ingest.md:29
msgid "A Tokio task is spawned per corpus, one per TMX release."
msgstr ""

#: src/getting-started/first-ingest.md:30
msgid ""
"Each task downloads (with retry/backoff), decompresses gzip, and streams the "
"file through `quick-xml`."
msgstr ""

#: src/getting-started/first-ingest.md:32
msgid ""
"A bounded mpsc channel (capacity 1000) feeds parsed pairs to a writer task, "
"which batches them in groups of 1000 and writes them transactionally."
msgstr ""

#: src/getting-started/first-ingest.md:34
msgid ""
"SIGINT and SIGTERM trigger a graceful shutdown; in-flight batches finish "
"before exit."
msgstr ""

#: src/getting-started/first-ingest.md:37
msgid ""
"Progress bars appear during download. When a file completes you will see a "
"log line like `Ingested 12345 items from es_OpenSubtitles.tmx`."
msgstr ""

#: src/getting-started/first-ingest.md:40
msgid "3. Inspect the data"
msgstr ""

#: src/getting-started/first-ingest.md:43
msgid ""
"\"$WISECROW__DB_URL\" <<'SQL'\n"
"SELECT count(*) FROM translations;\n"
"SELECT count(*) FROM languages;\n"
"SELECT from_phrase, to_phrase, frequency\n"
"  FROM translations\n"
"  ORDER BY frequency DESC\n"
"  LIMIT 10;\n"
"SQL\n"
msgstr ""

#: src/getting-started/first-ingest.md:53
msgid ""
"The most frequent rows tend to be short stop-word phrases: this is normal "
"and exactly the signal SRS card selection relies on."
msgstr ""

#: src/getting-started/first-ingest.md:56
msgid "4. Start a learning session"
msgstr ""

