#: src/guides/frequency-ranking.md:3
msgid ""
"Wisecrow is built on the premise that frequency drives fluency, so the order "
"in which cards reach you is not a cosmetic detail — it is the product. This "
"guide covers where that ordering comes from, why a freshly ingested corpus "
"produces almost no cards until it has been ranked, and what to do for "
"languages whose frequency lists nobody has published."
msgstr ""

#: src/guides/frequency-ranking.md:9
msgid "Why ranking is a required step"
msgstr ""

#: src/guides/frequency-ranking.md:11
msgid ""
"Ingestion sets each new translation's `frequency` to 1 and increments it "
"when the same pair arrives again, so the column starts as a duplicate count "
"rather than a measure of commonality. Deck selection then asks for rows with "
"`frequency > 1`, which means a corpus ingested once and never ranked offers "
"the learner almost nothing: on a 25,000-pair Welsh sample, ten rows cleared "
"that filter. Running `frequency` is what turns a pile of aligned sentences "
"into an ordered curriculum."
msgstr ""

#: src/guides/frequency-ranking.md:23
msgid ""
"With no `--file`, the command fetches the Hermit Dave FrequencyWords list "
"for the language, which is derived from OpenSubtitles and covers 62 "
"languages."
msgstr ""

#: src/guides/frequency-ranking.md:26
msgid "What a list can and cannot reach"
msgstr ""

#: src/guides/frequency-ranking.md:28
msgid ""
"Two properties of the matching are worth understanding before you judge the "
"results, because both bound how much of a corpus a list can touch."
msgstr ""

#: src/guides/frequency-ranking.md:31
msgid ""
"The first is that matching applies to **whole phrases**. A list holds single "
"words; a subtitle corpus holds sentences. A row is ranked only when its "
"entire phrase equals a listed word, so a word list reaches the single-word "
"rows and leaves the sentences alone. On the Welsh sample above, 749 of "
"25,000 rows were single words. This is a real ceiling, not a defect to work "
"around: sentence-level ranking would need a scoring function over each row's "
"tokens."
msgstr ""

#: src/guides/frequency-ranking.md:38
msgid ""
"The second is that matching **folds case and edge punctuation**. Corpus "
"phrases arrive as `Beth` and `O.` where lists hold `beth` and `o`, and "
"comparing them raw would discard most of the overlap. Both sides are "
"lower-cased and stripped of leading and trailing `.,!?;:\"'¡¿` before "
"comparison. Migration `016_normalised_phrase_indexes.sql` maintains "
"expression indexes over exactly that normalisation, so the update stays "
"index-driven; if you change the character set in `frequency.rs`, change the "
"migration to match, and a unit test will hold you to it."
msgstr ""

#: src/guides/frequency-ranking.md:47
msgid "Either side of the pair"
msgstr ""

#: src/guides/frequency-ranking.md:49
msgid ""
"A list ranks a translation from whichever side of the pair its language sits "
"on. A Welsh list therefore reaches rows ingested as `-n en -f cy`, where "
"Welsh is the target, just as it reaches rows ingested as `-n cy -f en`. "
"Ingest direction is irrelevant, which matters because the ordinary direction "
"for an English speaker studying Welsh puts Welsh in `to_phrase`."
msgstr ""

#: src/guides/frequency-ranking.md:55
msgid ""
"One consequence follows from a row carrying a single `frequency` column: if "
"you apply lists for both languages of a pair, the later application wins. "
"Rank by the language you are studying, and apply the other only if you want "
"the deck ordered by the prompt language instead."
msgstr ""

#: src/guides/frequency-ranking.md:60
msgid "Languages Hermit Dave does not cover"
msgstr ""

#: src/guides/frequency-ranking.md:62
msgid ""
"Welsh, Irish and Scottish Gaelic are all absent from the FrequencyWords "
"collection, so `frequency --lang cy` fails with a 404 and `--file` becomes "
"the only route. The [Leipzig Corpora "
"Collection](https://wortschatz.uni-leipzig.de/en/download) fills the gap for "
"two of the three, and its word files are read in their native layout without "
"reshaping:"
msgstr ""

#: src/guides/frequency-ranking.md:76
msgid ""
"Leipzig publishes Welsh (`cym`) and Irish (`gle`) Wikipedia corpora but no "
"Scottish Gaelic one, which the next two sections address."
msgstr ""

#: src/guides/frequency-ranking.md:79
msgid ""
"`--file` accepts three layouts, choosing per line rather than per file, so a "
"list carrying comment rows or a stray blank causes no trouble:"
msgstr ""

#: src/guides/frequency-ranking.md:82 src/reference/cli-reference.md:137
msgid "Layout"
msgstr ""

#: src/guides/frequency-ranking.md:82 src/reference/cli-reference.md:137
msgid "Shape"
msgstr ""

#: src/guides/frequency-ranking.md:82
msgid "Typical source"
msgstr ""

#: src/guides/frequency-ranking.md:84 src/reference/cli-reference.md:139
msgid "`word count`"
msgstr ""

#: src/guides/frequency-ranking.md:84
msgid "space-separated, two fields"
msgstr ""

#: src/guides/frequency-ranking.md:84
msgid "Hermit Dave FrequencyWords"
msgstr ""

#: src/guides/frequency-ranking.md:85 src/reference/cli-reference.md:140
msgid "`rank<TAB>word<TAB>count`"
msgstr ""

#: src/guides/frequency-ranking.md:85
msgid "tab-separated, three fields"
msgstr ""

#: src/guides/frequency-ranking.md:85 src/reference/cli-reference.md:140
msgid "Leipzig Corpora Collection"
msgstr ""

#: src/guides/frequency-ranking.md:86 src/reference/cli-reference.md:141
msgid "`word,count`"
msgstr ""

#: src/guides/frequency-ranking.md:86
msgid "comma-separated, trailing comma tolerated"
msgstr ""

#: src/guides/frequency-ranking.md:86 src/reference/cli-reference.md:141
msgid "published CSV lists"
msgstr ""

#: src/guides/frequency-ranking.md:88
msgid ""
"A line is accepted under the first layout whose count parses as a number, "
"which keeps a `word count` entry containing a comma from being mangled by "
"the CSV rule. Anything matching none of the three is skipped, and a file "
"that yields no entries at all is rejected rather than reported as a "
"successful update of nothing."
msgstr ""

#: src/guides/frequency-ranking.md:94
msgid "Scottish Gaelic"
msgstr ""

#: src/guides/frequency-ranking.md:96
msgid ""
"Gaelic is absent from both of the usual collections, but two community lists "
"exist. "
"[`innesmck/GaelicFrequencyLists`](https://github.com/innesmck/GaelicFrequencyLists) "
"is the better of them: 10,000 word forms with counts, MIT licensed, built "
"from LearnGaelic's _Litir do Luchd-ionnsachaidh_ and _Watch Gaelic_ BBC ALBA "
"transcripts. It counts surface forms rather than lemmas, which is what the "
"matcher wants, and its CSV loads without conversion:"
msgstr ""

#: src/guides/frequency-ranking.md:108
msgid ""
"A second list from "
"[iGàidhlig](http://www.igaidhlig.net/en/gaelic-word-frequencies/) offers "
"12,800 forms drawn from a web corpus, but it ships as an ODS spreadsheet "
"with the columns reversed, states no licence, and skews towards "
"institutional vocabulary. Prefer the first."
msgstr ""

#: src/guides/frequency-ranking.md:113
msgid "Deriving a list from the corpus"
msgstr ""

#: src/guides/frequency-ranking.md:115
msgid ""
"Where no list exists, or where a published one comes from the wrong genre, "
"the ingested corpus can supply its own counts:"
msgstr ""

#: src/guides/frequency-ranking.md:122
msgid ""
"This tokenises every phrase stored for the language, counts the word forms, "
"and applies the result through the same matching path a file would take. Two "
"things recommend it. The counts describe the material actually being studied "
"rather than a corpus of another register, and the vocabulary matches by "
"construction, since every word counted came from a phrase already in the "
"table. Measured on the OpenSubtitles Gaelic release, it ranked 725 rows "
"where the best published Gaelic list reached 369."
msgstr ""

#: src/guides/frequency-ranking.md:130
msgid ""
"It changes where the counts come from, not what they can rank: matching "
"remains whole-phrase, so this ranks single-word rows and leaves the "
"sentences containing those words alone. A tokeniser is required, so Khmer, "
"Lao and Burmese are refused rather than mis-segmented."
msgstr ""

#: src/guides/frequency-ranking.md:135
msgid "Checking the result"
msgstr ""

#: src/guides/frequency-ranking.md:137
msgid ""
"The command reports how many rows it updated, and the count of rows that "
"clear the deck filter is the figure that matters:"
msgstr ""

#: src/guides/frequency-ranking.md:146
msgid ""
"If the update reports zero, work through three causes in order: the language "
"has no row in `languages` at all, in which case the command logs a warning "
"and does nothing; the list parsed but nothing matched, which on a sentence "
"corpus with a word list is expected to be a small fraction; or the file was "
"in neither supported layout, which is now an error rather than a silent "
"success."
msgstr ""

