msgid "`--format`"
msgstr ""

#: src/guides/graded-reader.md:34
msgid "`md`"
msgstr ""

#: src/guides/graded-reader.md:34
msgid "Output format: `md` (Markdown) or `html` (self-contained HTML page)."
msgstr ""

#: src/guides/graded-reader.md:35
msgid "`--output`"
msgstr ""

#: src/guides/graded-reader.md:35
msgid "stdout"
msgstr ""

#: src/guides/graded-reader.md:35
msgid "Write to a file instead of stdout."
msgstr ""

#: src/guides/graded-reader.md:37
msgid "How \"learned\" is defined"
msgstr ""

#: src/guides/graded-reader.md:39
msgid ""
"The seed-vocab query (`VocabularyQuery::learned`) joins `cards` against "
"`translations` filtered by:"
msgstr ""

#: src/guides/graded-reader.md:42
msgid ""
"`cards.state = ANY($seed_states)` — defaults to `[2]` (FSRS Review state)."
msgstr ""

#: src/guides/graded-reader.md:43
msgid ""
"Optional `cards.stability >= $seed_min_stability` — extra filter for \"I've "
"actually internalised this,\" not just \"FSRS marked it Review.\""
msgstr ""

#: src/guides/graded-reader.md:45
msgid ""
"Ordered by `translations.frequency DESC` — corpus-frequency ranking so the "
"most useful learned words seed the passage."
msgstr ""

#: src/guides/graded-reader.md:48
msgid "This means:"
msgstr ""

#: src/guides/graded-reader.md:50
msgid ""
"A fresh `wisecrow learn` user will get an empty seed list and the command "
"will error with `No learned vocabulary found for the given filters`."
msgstr ""

#: src/guides/graded-reader.md:52
msgid ""
"The seed list is **language-pair-agnostic per user — currently** (see "
"Limitations)."
msgstr ""

#: src/guides/graded-reader.md:55
msgid "Output formats"
msgstr ""

#: src/guides/graded-reader.md:57
msgid "**Markdown** (`--format md`):"
msgstr ""

#: src/guides/graded-reader.md:70
msgid "**HTML** (`--format html`):"
msgstr ""

#: src/guides/graded-reader.md:72
msgid ""
"A self-contained `<!doctype html>` page with `<h1>`/`<p>`/`<h2>`/`<ul>`. "
"User content is HTML-escaped (`&`, `<`, `>`, `\"`). No external CSS or JS — "
"open the file in any browser. Pipe to a printer-CSS preprocessor for print "
"output, or render via `pandoc` for PDF."
msgstr ""

#: src/guides/graded-reader.md:77
msgid "Tips"
msgstr ""

#: src/guides/graded-reader.md:79
msgid ""
"Use `--seed-min-stability` once you've been learning for a while to avoid "
"the LLM being \"fed\" cards you technically passed once but haven't actually "
"retained."
msgstr ""

#: src/guides/graded-reader.md:82
msgid ""
"For a denser passage, raise `--seed-limit` (more vocabulary diversity) and "
"`--length-words` together."
msgstr ""

#: src/guides/graded-reader.md:84
msgid ""
"For a more challenging text, set the CEFR level one notch above your comfort "
"zone and pass a larger `--seed-limit` so the LLM has more to work with."
msgstr ""

#: src/guides/graded-reader.md:90
msgid ""
"v1 operates on a single-user assumption: the `cards` table has no `user_id`. "
"\"Learned\" means \"any card row in this state, regardless of who reviewed "
"it.\" Multi-user-aware semantics is a follow-up."
msgstr ""

#: src/guides/graded-reader.md:93
msgid ""
"Quality depends on the LLM. The first paragraph is usually best; later "
"paragraphs sometimes drift in style or introduce more new vocabulary than "
"asked."
msgstr ""

#: src/guides/graded-reader.md:96
msgid ""
"Length is approximate — the LLM may overshoot or undershoot `--length-words` "
"by ~30%."
msgstr ""

#: src/guides/preview-subtitles.md:3
msgid ""
"`wisecrow preview --file <path>` parses an `.srt`, `.vtt`, `.ass`, or `.ssa` "
"subtitle file, tokenises the text, and produces an annotated frequency table "
"showing which words you already know, which you're currently learning, and "
"which are entirely new."
msgstr ""

#: src/guides/preview-subtitles.md:10
msgid ""
"You're about to watch tonight's episode of a show in your target language "
"and want to triage vocabulary first."
msgstr ""

#: src/guides/preview-subtitles.md:12
msgid ""
"You want to know which lemmata in a script are corpus-rare so you can "
"pre-load them as cards before they ambush you."
msgstr ""

#: src/guides/preview-subtitles.md:21
msgid "Alias: `wisecrow pv ...`."
msgstr ""

#: src/guides/preview-subtitles.md:25 src/reference/cli-reference.md:104
#: src/reference/cli-reference.md:129
