#: src/guides/preview-subtitles.md:43
msgid ""
"Correct for ~90 languages: Latin, Cyrillic, Arabic, Devanagari, Hangul "
"(eojeol-level), etc."
msgstr ""

#: src/guides/preview-subtitles.md:45
msgid "Annotation legend"
msgstr ""

#: src/guides/preview-subtitles.md:47
msgid "Each token is tagged with one of:"
msgstr ""

#: src/guides/preview-subtitles.md:49
msgid ""
"`[known]` — present in `translations` AND has a `cards` row in FSRS state 2 "
"(Review). You've internalised this word."
msgstr ""

#: src/guides/preview-subtitles.md:50
msgid ""
"`[learning]` — present in `translations` AND has a `cards` row in FSRS state "
"1 (Learning) or 3 (Relearning)."
msgstr ""

#: src/guides/preview-subtitles.md:51
msgid ""
"`[new]` — present in `translations` AND has either no `cards` row, or a row "
"in state 0 (New)."
msgstr ""

#: src/guides/preview-subtitles.md:52
msgid ""
"`[?]` — not present in `translations` for this language pair. You haven't "
"ingested this word, the corpus doesn't contain it, or it's an inflected form "
"not in the corpus's surface-form index."
msgstr ""

#: src/guides/preview-subtitles.md:54
msgid "Status semantics"
msgstr ""

#: src/guides/preview-subtitles.md:56
msgid ""
"Output is sorted by corpus frequency descending. With `--top-n 30` you get "
"the 30 highest-frequency tokens in the file. With `--unknown-only`, only "
"`[new]` and `[?]` tokens are included — that's \"what does this script "
"demand of me that I haven't yet drilled.\""
msgstr ""

#: src/guides/preview-subtitles.md:61
msgid "LLM gloss for corpus-unknowns"
msgstr ""

#: src/guides/preview-subtitles.md:63
msgid ""
"`--gloss-unknowns` collects all `[?]` tokens (those completely missing from "
"the `translations` table for this language pair), sends them to the LLM in "
"one batch with a \"translate these foreign words to <native>\" prompt, and "
"appends the returned gloss inline:"
msgstr ""

#: src/guides/preview-subtitles.md:73
msgid ""
"This catches words from the script that your corpus simply doesn't cover — "
"inflected forms not in the surface-form index, slang, names, or rare lemmata."
msgstr ""

#: src/guides/preview-subtitles.md:76
msgid ""
"`--gloss-unknowns` requires `WISECROW__LLM_PROVIDER` and "
"`WISECROW__LLM_API_KEY` set; without them the CLI errors fast."
msgstr ""

#: src/guides/preview-subtitles.md:79
msgid "Examples"
msgstr ""

#: src/guides/preview-subtitles.md:82
msgid "# Triage tonight's Spanish episode, top 30 unknowns.\n"
