#: src/reference/architecture.md:1
msgid "Architecture overview"
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/architecture.md:3
msgid ""
"Wisecrow is a Cargo workspace with one production crate (`wisecrow-core`) "
"and three satellite crates that share types through `wisecrow-dto`. Almost "
"every behaviour you can invoke from the CLI is also reachable as a library "
"function, so the `bin/wisecrow.rs` entry point is intentionally a thin "
"orchestration layer."
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/architecture.md:9
msgid "Workspace layout"
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/architecture.md:37
msgid "Crate responsibilities"
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/architecture.md:41
msgid ""
"The library half exposes the [`Langs`](../api/wisecrow-core.md#langs) "
"newtype, the `Ingester`, `SessionManager`, `CardManager`, `DnbEngine`, and "
"the `LlmProvider` trait. The binary half (`bin/wisecrow.rs`) parses CLI "
"args, constructs a connection pool, and dispatches to library functions."
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/architecture.md:48
msgid ""
"Plain serializable structs and enums (`CardDto`, `SessionDto`, "
"`DnbConfigDto`, `GrammarRuleDto`, …) plus a small `SpeedController` value "
"type used by the session UI. The crate has no database or framework "
"dependencies — it can be consumed by the WASM bundle and the mobile shell "
"without dragging in `wisecrow-core`."
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/architecture.md:56
msgid ""
"Dioxus 0.7 fullstack app. The `server` cargo feature gates everything that "
"needs the database; the WASM bundle ships only the UI components and routes "
"through Dioxus' `#[server]` server-functions. The router exposes `Home`, "
"`LearnPage`, `NbackPage`, and `QuizPage`."
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/architecture.md:63
msgid ""
"A skeleton mobile/desktop shell. The router is similar to the web crate but "
"the `server_fns.rs` are client-side stubs — the real implementations live in "
"`wisecrow-web` and are reached over HTTP."
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/architecture.md:67
msgid "Ingestion pipeline"
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/architecture.md:69
msgid ""
"Ingestion is the most complex flow in the system. It is a producer-consumer "
"pipeline over a bounded `tokio::sync::mpsc` channel."
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/architecture.md:97
msgid "Key constants and invariants:"
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/architecture.md:99
msgid ""
"**Channel bound** is `1000` (`ingesting::CHANNEL_BOUND`). Producers block "
"when the consumer cannot keep up — back-pressure is intentional."
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/architecture.md:101
msgid ""
"**Batch size** is `1000` (`ingesting::persisting::TRANSLATION_BATCH_SIZE`). "
"A smaller batch increases round-trips; a larger batch increases the lock "
"window."
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/architecture.md:103
msgid ""
"**Decompression** is bounded to 1 GiB (`MAX_DECOMPRESSED_BYTES`) to defuse "
"zip-bombs."
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/architecture.md:105
msgid ""
"**Path traversal** is blocked: ZIP entries that start with `/`, `\\`, or "
"contain `..` are dropped, and entries are rejected if they would "
"canonicalize outside the extraction root."
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/architecture.md:108
msgid ""
"**Idempotency**: `INSERT … ON CONFLICT DO UPDATE SET frequency = frequency + "
"1` makes re-ingestion deterministic and additive."
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/architecture.md:111
msgid "Spaced repetition"
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/architecture.md:113
msgid ""
"`wisecrow-core` uses [`rs-fsrs`](https://crates.io/crates/rs-fsrs) for the "
"algorithm. The wrapper at `srs::scheduler::CardManager` is responsible for:"
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/architecture.md:116
msgid "Enumerating due cards filtered by language pair."
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/architecture.md:117
msgid "Computing the next FSRS state from a `ReviewRating`."
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/architecture.md:118
msgid ""
"Persisting `stability`, `difficulty`, `state`, `due` back into PostgreSQL."
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/architecture.md:120
msgid ""
"Sessions in `srs::session::SessionManager` glue the deck together — they "
"select a fixed-size cohort of cards (due first, then unlearned vocabulary), "
"record positions in `session_cards`, and let the user pause and resume."
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/architecture.md:124
msgid ""
"The session selection ordering is deterministic and ranks **Relearning > "
"Learning > New > Review**, so cards in the riskiest states are surfaced "
"first."
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/architecture.md:129
msgid ""
"Independent of the SRS, the `dnb` module implements an adaptive dual n-back "
"trainer that uses the user's own vocabulary as audio + visual stimuli. It is "
"two systems welded together:"
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/architecture.md:133
msgid ""
"A pure scheduling core: `DnbEngine` generates trials, picks matches with a "
"fixed 30% probability, and avoids accidental matches when generating "
"non-match items."
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/architecture.md:136
msgid ""
"An adaptation layer: `scoring::apply_adaptation` updates `n_level` and "
"`interval_ms` every 5 trials based on the rolling accuracy window. It "
"terminates early when accuracy drops below 40% or after three consecutive "
"windows below the starting `n_level`."
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/architecture.md:141
msgid ""
"After a session the trial outcomes are folded back into the SRS "
"(`dnb::feedback::apply_srs_feedback`) — net-correct trials nudge cards "
"toward `Good`, net-incorrect toward `Again`."
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/architecture.md:145
msgid "LLM integration"
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/architecture.md:147
msgid "A minimal trait keeps providers swappable:"
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/architecture.md:157
msgid ""
"The factory `llm::create_provider` reads `llm_provider` and `llm_api_key` "
"from config and returns a boxed implementation. Two are bundled: `anthropic` "
"(Claude Sonnet) and `openai` (GPT-4o)."
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/architecture.md:161
msgid ""
"Prompts are deliberately strict (\"Return ONLY the JSON array\") and the "
"seeders/exercises tolerate fenced code-blocks (```` ```json ````) when "
"parsing the response."
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/architecture.md:165 src/reference/troubleshooting.md:188
msgid "Sync"
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/architecture.md:167
msgid ""
"`sync::SyncClient` walks three paginated endpoints on a remote Wisecrow "
"server:"
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/architecture.md:170
msgid "Mirrors"
msgstr ""

