msgid "`-l`, `--lang`"
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/cli-reference.md:128
msgid "Language whose words the list holds."
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/cli-reference.md:129
msgid "Read a local list instead of downloading Hermit Dave's."
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/cli-reference.md:130
msgid "`--from-corpus`"
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/cli-reference.md:130
msgid "Derive counts from the stored phrases; conflicts with `--file`."
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/cli-reference.md:132
msgid ""
"With neither flag the command fetches "
"`hermitdave/FrequencyWords/…/<code>/<code>_50k.txt`, which exists for 62 "
"languages and none of the Celtic ones. With `--file` it reads any of three "
"layouts, choosing per line rather than per file:"
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/cli-reference.md:139
msgid "space-separated pair"
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/cli-reference.md:139
msgid "Hermit Dave"
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/cli-reference.md:140
msgid "tab-separated triple"
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/cli-reference.md:141
msgid "comma-separated pair"
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/cli-reference.md:143
msgid ""
"`--from-corpus` needs no list at all: it tokenises the phrases already "
"stored for the language and counts the forms, which is the route for "
"languages nobody has published a list for. It requires a tokeniser for the "
"language."
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/cli-reference.md:147
msgid ""
"Matching folds case and strips edge punctuation (`.,!?;:\"'¡¿`), and applies "
"to whichever side of a pair holds the listed language, so ingest direction "
"is irrelevant. Only whole phrases match: a word list ranks single-word rows, "
"not the sentences containing that word. A file that parses to no entries is "
"an error rather than a silent no-op."
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/cli-reference.md:155
msgid "`learn`"
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/cli-reference.md:161
msgid ""
"Opens the flashcard TUI. Defaults: deck of 50 cards, 3000 ms auto-advance, "
"user ID 1."
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/cli-reference.md:166
msgid ""
"Number of cards in the session. Filled with due cards first, then unlearned "
"vocabulary by frequency."
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/cli-reference.md:167
msgid "Auto-advance interval in milliseconds; clamped to `[500, 10000]`."
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/cli-reference.md:168
msgid "Users are scoped per FK; create more with the schema `users` table."
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/cli-reference.md:170
msgid ""
"If a paused session exists for `(user_id, native, foreign)` it is resumed. "
"Press `q` to pause; the next invocation picks up at the same card index."
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/cli-reference.md:175
msgid "`nback`"
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/cli-reference.md:181
msgid ""
"Runs an adaptive dual n-back session using your stored vocabulary as "
"stimuli. Requires at least 8 ingested pairs for the language combination."
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/cli-reference.md:184
msgid "Values"
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/cli-reference.md:186
msgid "`audio_written`, `word_translation`, `audio_image`"
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/cli-reference.md:187
msgid "`1`–`9` (clamped to range)"
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/cli-reference.md:188
msgid "FK into `users`"
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/cli-reference.md:190
msgid ""
"Controls during a trial: `[A]` audio match, `[L]` visual match, `[Enter]` "
"submit, `[Q]` quit. The engine adapts every 5 trials and terminates early "
"when accuracy is consistently below 40 %."
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/cli-reference.md:196
msgid "`list-languages`"
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/cli-reference.md:202
msgid ""
"Prints the 102 supported language codes with their human-readable names. "
"Useful before invoking `ingest` to confirm a code."
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/cli-reference.md:213
msgid ""
"Generates grammar rules for the supplied CEFR levels via the configured LLM "
"provider. 15 rules are requested per level; the prompt asks for at least one "
"correct and one incorrect example per rule."
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/cli-reference.md:217 src/reference/cli-reference.md:331
#: src/reference/cli-reference.md:351
msgid "Requires `WISECROW__LLM_PROVIDER` and `WISECROW__LLM_API_KEY`."
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/cli-reference.md:227
msgid ""
"Imports grammar rules from a JSON file matching the "
"`wisecrow_dto::GrammarRuleImport` shape. The import flow is upsert by "
"`(language_id, cefr_level_id, title)` so re-running with corrected data is "
"safe."
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/cli-reference.md:232
msgid "Example file shape:"
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/cli-reference.md:237
msgid "\"Present tense of regular -ar verbs\""
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/cli-reference.md:238
msgid ""
"\"Spanish verbs ending in -ar follow a fixed pattern: drop -ar and add -o, "
"-as, -a, -amos, -áis, -an.\""
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/cli-reference.md:241
msgid "\"Hablo español.\""
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/cli-reference.md:241
msgid "\"I speak Spanish.\""
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/cli-reference.md:242
msgid "\"Hablamos español.\""
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/cli-reference.md:242
msgid "\"We speak Spanish.\""
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/cli-reference.md:256
msgid ""
"Extracts text from a PDF and stores each parsed rule with `source = 'pdf'`. "
"The extraction is best-effort — see [Grammar "
"workflows](../guides/grammar-workflows.md) for tips on cleaning the imported "
"rules."
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/cli-reference.md:262
msgid "`generate-exercises`"
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/cli-reference.md:268
msgid ""
"Generates a mix of cloze and multiple-choice quizzes from the stored grammar "
"rules at the chosen CEFR level. Requires the LLM configuration. The output "
"is printed to stdout (suitable for piping into `jq`)."
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/cli-reference.md:274
msgid "`--count`"
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/cli-reference.md:274 src/reference/cli-reference.md:290
msgid "`20`"
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/cli-reference.md:278
msgid "`quiz`"
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/cli-reference.md:284
msgid ""
"Reads a PDF, generates `N` quiz items inline, and runs them in the terminal. "
"This command does **not** require a database — it is the lightest path to "
"trying the quiz UI."
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/cli-reference.md:290
msgid "`--num-questions`"
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/cli-reference.md:294
msgid "`prefetch-media`"
msgstr ""

