#: src/reference/troubleshooting.md:10
msgid ""
"`Config::database_url` returns this when neither form A nor a _complete_ "
"form B is present. Common slip-ups:"
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/troubleshooting.md:13
msgid ""
"Missing `WISECROW__DB_PASSWORD` — easy to forget if you committed a `.env` "
"with the username but not the password."
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/troubleshooting.md:15
msgid "Wrong separator — must be `__` (double underscore)."
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/troubleshooting.md:16
msgid "A typo in the prefix. The loader is strict about `WISECROW__`."
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/troubleshooting.md:18
msgid "Check with:"
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/troubleshooting.md:24
msgid "`Configuration error: relative URL without a base`"
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/troubleshooting.md:26
msgid ""
"`config.rs` builds the URL from the components via `url::Url::parse(...)`. A "
"bare host like `localhost` works; a host with a slash inside it (or a "
"trailing colon without a port) fails."
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/troubleshooting.md:32
msgid "`Persistence migration error`"
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/troubleshooting.md:34
msgid ""
"The migrations are embedded into the binary. The error wraps a "
"`sqlx::migrate::MigrateError`; the most common causes are:"
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/troubleshooting.md:37
msgid "The user lacks `CREATE TABLE` — Wisecrow needs DDL privileges."
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/troubleshooting.md:38
msgid ""
"A previous custom migration left `_sqlx_migrations` in an inconsistent "
"state. `SELECT * FROM _sqlx_migrations ORDER BY version` shows the log; "
"truncating it is destructive — only do it on a database you can recreate."
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/troubleshooting.md:41
msgid ""
"The PostgreSQL version is \\< 12. The bulk-insert path uses `unnest(..., "
"...)` which requires PG ≥ 12."
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/troubleshooting.md:44
msgid "`relation \"sessions\" does not exist`"
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/troubleshooting.md:46
msgid "The pool was opened against the wrong database. Sanity-check with:"
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/troubleshooting.md:49
msgid "\"\\\\dt\""
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/troubleshooting.md:52
msgid ""
"If the table list is empty, run any database-touching command (e.g. "
"`wisecrow ingest`) — migrations run on first connection."
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/troubleshooting.md:55
msgid "Ingest"
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/troubleshooting.md:57
msgid "Stuck on a single file forever"
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/troubleshooting.md:59
msgid ""
"The retry loop sleeps `2^attempt` seconds. With `max_retries = 3` the worst "
"case is 14 s of back-off plus three full reads. If you see no progress at "
"all, inspect with `wisecrow=trace` logging — you will see the chunk-loop "
"lines."
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/troubleshooting.md:64
msgid "`HTTP 404 Not Found`"
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/troubleshooting.md:66
msgid "Not every language pair exists in every corpus. Try:"
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/troubleshooting.md:72
msgid ""
"If 404s keep coming, drop `--corpus` and let Wisecrow attempt the others. "
"The CLI continues on per-file errors."
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/troubleshooting.md:75
msgid "`File too large: ... bytes (max: ...)`"
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/troubleshooting.md:77
msgid ""
"The `--max-file-size-mb` ceiling triggered. Either bump it explicitly or "
"split your ingest by corpus:"
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/troubleshooting.md:84
msgid "`No frequency entries parsed from ...`"
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/troubleshooting.md:86
msgid ""
"The file was in none of the supported layouts. `--file` reads `word count` "
"pairs (Hermit Dave), `rank<TAB>word<TAB>count` triples (Leipzig) and "
"`word,count` CSV; a list of bare words with no counts matches none of them. "
"Check the separator first, since a tab-separated file that has been through "
"an editor may have had its tabs expanded to spaces."
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/troubleshooting.md:92
msgid "`frequency` reports `Updated 0 ...`"
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/troubleshooting.md:94
msgid "The file parsed, but nothing matched. In order of likelihood:"
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/troubleshooting.md:96
msgid ""
"The language has no row in `languages`. The command logs a warning saying "
"so; ingest a corpus for it first."
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/troubleshooting.md:98
msgid ""
"Nothing overlapped. Word lists rank whole single-word rows only, so on a "
"sentence-aligned corpus a small fraction is the expected outcome — see "
"[Frequency ranking](../guides/frequency-ranking.md). If the list comes from "
"a different genre to the corpus, `--from-corpus` will reach more rows."
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/troubleshooting.md:103
msgid "`Decompressed output exceeds the ... byte limit`"
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/troubleshooting.md:105
msgid ""
"The `--max-decompressed-mb` ceiling (default `8192`) triggered while "
"expanding the archive. This is a separate limit from `--max-file-size-mb`, "
"which governs only the transfer; corpus TMX compresses four- or five-fold, "
"so a download well inside the transfer ceiling can still overrun this one. "
"Raise it to suit the release and the disk you have:"
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/troubleshooting.md:115
msgid ""
"The partially-written output is deleted before the error is returned, so "
"there is nothing to clean up beyond the downloaded archive itself."
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/troubleshooting.md:118
msgid "Inserts plateau under load"
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/troubleshooting.md:120
msgid ""
"`DatabasePersister::consume` flushes in batches of 1000 inside a single "
"transaction. If your PG instance is small, a parallel ingest of multiple "
"language pairs can pile up. Solutions:"
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/troubleshooting.md:124
msgid "Reduce concurrency by serialising the calls (one pair at a time)."
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/troubleshooting.md:125
msgid "Bump `max_connections` in `postgresql.conf`."
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/troubleshooting.md:126
msgid ""
"Pre-warm `random_page_cost`, `shared_buffers`, and disable "
"`synchronous_commit` for the duration of the ingest."
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/troubleshooting.md:131
msgid "\"No cards available. Ingest some data first with `wisecrow ingest`.\""
msgstr ""

