#: src/reference/translating.md:1
msgid "Translating the documentation"
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/translating.md:3
msgid ""
"This book is translated with "
"[Gettext](https://www.gnu.org/software/gettext/), the same machinery used "
"for translating software, by way of "
"[`mdbook-i18n-helpers`](https://github.com/google/mdbook-i18n-helpers). The "
"arrangement is worth explaining before the commands, because it determines "
"what a translator actually edits."
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/translating.md:9
msgid "How it fits together"
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/translating.md:11
msgid ""
"The English Markdown under `src/` is the single source of truth, and it is "
"never duplicated. Instead, every translatable string is extracted into a "
"template, `po/messages.pot`, and each language keeps its own catalogue of "
"translations at `po/<lang>.po` pairing each English string with its "
"rendering. At build time the `gettext` preprocessor substitutes the strings "
"for the requested language; anything left untranslated falls back to the "
"English, so a partial translation produces a usable book rather than a "
"broken one."
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/translating.md:19
msgid "This is why the configuration in `book.toml` is so small:"
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/translating.md:21
msgid ""
"```toml\n"
"[preprocessor.gettext]\n"
"after = [\"links\"]\n"
"```"
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/translating.md:26
msgid ""
"Running after the `links` preprocessor matters: it means any file pulled in "
"by an include directive is translated along with the file that includes it, "
"rather than being skipped."
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/translating.md:30
msgid ""
"The preprocessor is a no-op when building the source language, so the "
"ordinary `mdbook build` is unaffected by any of this."
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/translating.md:35
msgid ""
"The devshell provides everything already. Outside it, you need `mdbook`, the "
"helpers, and GNU Gettext's command-line tools:"
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/translating.md:42
msgid "Starting a new translation"
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/translating.md:44
msgid ""
"Create the catalogue from the template, naming it for the language code — "
"`gd` for Scottish Gaelic, `cy` for Welsh, and so on:"
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/translating.md:52
msgid ""
"Then edit `po/gd.po`, filling in the `msgstr` entries. Leave anything you "
"are unsure of empty and it will render in English."
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/translating.md:55
msgid "Building a translation"
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/translating.md:58
msgid "gd"
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/translating.md:61
msgid ""
"The result lands in `book/gd/`, alongside the English book in `book/`. CI "
"does this automatically for every `po/*.po` file it finds, so a new "
"translation needs no pipeline changes — adding the file is enough."
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/translating.md:65
msgid "Keeping catalogues current"
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/translating.md:67
msgid ""
"The template goes stale as soon as the English text changes, so regenerate "
"it and merge the differences into each language:"
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/translating.md:72
msgid "'{\"xgettext\": {}}'"
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/translating.md:76
msgid ""
"`msgmerge` preserves existing translations, marks those whose source text "
"has changed as fuzzy for review, and adds the new strings as untranslated. "
"Doing this in the same commit as a substantial documentation change spares "
"translators from reconstructing what moved."
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/contributing.md:3
msgid ""
"Wisecrow is a small project with strong conventions. This page distils the "
"ones you need to follow before submitting a patch."
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/contributing.md:6
msgid "Tooling"
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/contributing.md:8
msgid "Tool"
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/contributing.md:10
msgid "`cargo build` / `cargo check`"
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/contributing.md:10
msgid "Verify the workspace compiles."
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/contributing.md:11
msgid "`cargo nextest run`"
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/contributing.md:11
msgid "Run the test suite (fall back to `cargo test` if you don't have nextest)."
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/contributing.md:12
msgid "`cargo clippy --workspace --all-targets`"
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/contributing.md:12
msgid ""
"The codebase is required to be clippy-clean — no `#[allow]` annotations are "
"acceptable."
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/contributing.md:13
msgid "`cargo fmt --all`"
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/contributing.md:13
msgid "The repository is `rustfmt`\\-formatted."
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/contributing.md:15
msgid ""
"A pre-commit hook is wired through `pre-commit-config.yaml`; install "
"[`pre-commit`](https://pre-commit.com/) and run `pre-commit install` to get "
"the hooks locally."
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/contributing.md:19
msgid "Workspace conventions"
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/contributing.md:21
msgid "These rules live in the project's `CLAUDE.md` and are enforced in review:"
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/contributing.md:23
msgid ""
"**No `as` numeric casts.** Use `try_from`, `into`, or `From`. Compile-time "
"literals are the only exception."
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/contributing.md:25
msgid ""
"**No silent error discards.** `let _ = expr_returning_Result` is a bug. "
"Either propagate with `?` or log with `tracing::warn!`."
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/contributing.md:27
msgid ""
"**No `unreachable!()` outside tests.** \"Should never happen\" branches "
"still return `Err`."
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/contributing.md:29
msgid ""
"**Justify every `.clone()`.** Production clones must carry an inline `// "
"clone: <reason>` comment. Tests are exempt."
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/contributing.md:31
msgid ""
"**Use `Url` for URL construction.** Never `format!()` URLs — that is how "
"double-slash bugs are born."
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/contributing.md:33
msgid ""
"**`unwrap`/`expect`/`panic!` are forbidden** in async tasks and HTTP "
"handlers. Convert to `?`."
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/contributing.md:36
msgid "Test hierarchy"
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/contributing.md:38
msgid "Pick the test type _before_ writing it:"
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/contributing.md:40
msgid ""
"**Property-based (`proptest`)** — pure functions, parsers, validators, "
"serializers. The first choice for anything with an invariant."
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/contributing.md:42
msgid ""
"**Parameterised (`rstest`)** — bounded enum exhaustion or fewer than ~10 "
"specific cases."
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/contributing.md:44
msgid "**Standalone** — only when you genuinely need bespoke setup or mocking."
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/contributing.md:46
msgid ""
"Do not write a standalone test \"to get it working\" with the intent of "
"converting it later. The conversion never happens."
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/contributing.md:49
msgid ""
"Tests live alongside the code in `#[cfg(test)] mod tests` blocks. Use "
"`tests/` directories only for crate-spanning integration tests."
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/contributing.md:52
msgid "Database changes"
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/contributing.md:54
msgid ""
"New migrations go in `wisecrow-core/migrations/` numbered sequentially "
"(`0NN_short_name.sql`)."
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/contributing.md:56
msgid ""
"Migrations run automatically on first connection, so the workspace's tests "
"must be runnable against a fresh database."
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/contributing.md:58
msgid ""
"Always include the matching `DROP` semantics by relying on `ON DELETE "
"CASCADE` rather than ad-hoc cleanup."
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/contributing.md:61
msgid "Documentation changes"
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/contributing.md:63
msgid ""
"Public types should have rustdoc comments (`///`). Document `# Errors` and "
"`# Panics` sections where they apply."
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/contributing.md:65
msgid ""
"This mdBook (`docs/`) is not auto-generated; if you change a CLI surface or "
"a library type, update the relevant page in `docs/src/`."
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/contributing.md:67
msgid ""
"Code examples in this book are not currently doctested. Keep them small and "
"obviously correct; copy them from real source where possible."
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/contributing.md:70
msgid "Commit messages"
msgstr ""

